T07 optional DCA and bootstrap uncertainty addition — 2026-11-06

- Implemented descriptive decision curve analysis at 5% through 40%
  threshold probabilities in 1-point steps. For every target/threshold, the
  table records frozen-model net benefit plus treat-all and treat-none
  references. Three target-specific plots and a combined CSV are included.
  These calculations use only the one evaluation sample and do not select or
  modify the frozen T06 operating thresholds.
- Added deterministic paired row-bootstrap percentile 95% intervals for
  AUROC and average precision. The production protocol uses 1,000 replicates
  with seed 42; single-class draws are omitted from metric intervals and
  counted explicitly. Replicate count, seed, method, and invalid-draw policy
  are recorded in the run manifest and report.
- Added focused synthetic tests for net-benefit arithmetic and reference
  strategies, fixed threshold coverage, bootstrap determinism, valid/invalid
  draw accounting, and end-to-end output completeness/report/manifest fields.
  No model, calibrator, or threshold is refit or selected by these diagnostics.
